lass=\"eb-sep\"> · </span><span class=\"eb-name\">Established public listed companies</span>", "section": "One narrative. Two audiences. One disclosure gate.", "count": 1}, {"k": "db9ca5dd25", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "h1", "cls": "", "html": "One narrative. Two audiences. One disclosure gate.", "section": "One narrative. Two audiences. One disclosure gate.", "count": 1}, {"k": "d061d6d76a", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "p", "cls": "", "html": "In practice: one approved company story, one sign-off route your board controls, one calendar for investor and media releases, and a quarterly check on what the market actually heard. IR and PR run as a single engine, alongside the advisers and in-house team you already have.", "section": "One narrative. Two audiences. One disclosure gate.", "count": 1}, {"k": "506ba5e474", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "span", "cls": "eyebrow", "html": "Established PLC", "section": "Why companies that have been listed for years come to Aegis.", "count": 1}, {"k": "8564a05c7e", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "h2", "cls": "", "html": "Why companies that have been listed for years come to Aegis.", "section": "Why companies that have been listed for years come to Aegis.", "count": 1}, {"k": "1671d2bd37", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "p", "cls": "lede", "html": "The listing is long done. The question is whether the market still understands the company it has become.", "section": "Why companies that have been listed for years come to Aegis.", "count": 1}, {"k": "9983191a60", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "h4", "cls": "", "html": "Valuation gap versus peers", "section": "Why companies that have been listed for years come to Aegis.", "count": 1}, {"k": "0dd05e93e3", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "p", "cls": "", "html": "Results are sound, but the share price trails the sector. The company has changed and the market has not been told the new story.", "section": "Why companies that have been listed for years come to Aegis.", "count": 1}, {"k": "ba13a34a2f", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "h4", "cls": "", "html": "Research coverage lapsed", "section": "Why companies that have been listed for years come to Aegis.", "count": 1}, {"k": "4b9bf5401c", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "p", "cls": "", "html": "The analysts who covered you at listing have moved on. Fund managers no longer get an independent view of what the company is worth.", "section": "Why companies that have been listed for years come to Aegis.", "count": 1}, {"k": "e72e64d4f7", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "h4", "cls": "", "html": "Register has gone stale", "section": "Why companies that have been listed for years come to Aegis.", "count": 1}, {"k": "5911f38093", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "p", "cls": "", "html": "Few institutional holders, no foreign funds, and shares that trade thinly. Nobody has taken the company to local and regional funds in years.", "section": "Why companies that have been listed for years come to Aegis.", "count": 1}, {"k": "05d7ca0cdd", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "h4", "cls": "", "html": "A corporate exercise ahead", "section": "Why companies that have been listed for years come to Aegis.", "count": 1}, {"k": "6cae29d7d8", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "p", "cls": "", "html": "An acquisition, a placement, a new business line, a Main Market transfer or a rebrand. Each needs a message that lawyers will clear and the market will understand.", "section": "Why companies that have been listed for years come to Aegis.", "count": 1}, {"k": "b4462d7d7e", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "h4", "cls": "", "html": "A reputation issue", "section": "Why companies that have been listed for years come to Aegis.", "count": 1}, {"k": "4ca3065537", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "p", "cls": "", "html": "A Bursa query, a bad headline, a forum thread. Nobody owns the response, and the first 24 hours decide the story.", "section": "Why companies that have been listed for years come to Aegis.", "count": 1}, {"k": "ce6a5fa7a9", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "h4", "cls": "", "html": "In-house team stretched", "section": "Why companies that have been listed for years come to Aegis.", "count": 1}, {"k": "21812121b0", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "p", "cls": "", "html": "Corporate communications is one person, or the CFO on top of the day job. Results season and the AGM arrive regardless.", "section": "Why companies that have been listed for years come to Aegis.", "count": 1}, {"k": "54acc2806d", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "span", "cls": "num", "html": "Start here", "section": "Why companies that have been listed for years come to Aegis.", "count": 1}, {"k": "c724fdf0ab", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "h3", "cls": "", "html": "Begin with a perception audit.", "section": "Why companies that have been listed for years come to Aegis.", "count": 1}, {"k": "1816544854", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "p", "cls": "", "html": "Before any programme, Aegis talks to your investors, analysts, media and staff, scores your risk profile and maps who holds your shares and who else matters. You see how the market reads you today, then decide what to do next. If you already have advisers, this is the simplest way to start.", "section": "Why companies that have been listed for years come to Aegis.", "count": 1}, {"k": "a4fb74218c", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "a", "cls": "btn btn-primary", "html": "Request a perception audit", "section": "Why companies that have been listed for years come to Aegis.", "count": 2}, {"k": "37b0b58188", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "span", "cls": "num", "html": "Working with your in-house team", "section": "Why companies that have been listed for years come to Aegis.", "count": 1}, {"k": "ecb6fe10af", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "h3", "cls": "", "html": "Alongside, or in place of.", "section": "Why companies that have been listed for years come to Aegis.", "count": 1}, {"k": "5359c539e3", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "p", "cls": "", "html": "If you have a corporate communications or IR team, Aegis works inside it: one shared playbook, message bank and approval matrix, and one contact on each side. If you have none, Aegis acts as that team and reports to the CEO and CFO. Either way, you get experienced advice directly, with no layers and no handoffs.", "section": "Why companies that have been listed for years come to Aegis.", "count": 1}, {"k": "b32198a8e4", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "span", "cls": "eyebrow", "html": "Integrated IR + PR engagement model", "section": "The narrative spine.", "count": 1}, {"k": "c58dcffdd5", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "h2", "cls": "", "html": "The narrative spine.", "section": "The narrative spine.", "count": 1}, {"k": "2c75eeecc8", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "p", "cls": "lede", "html": "Bursa-listed or IPO-bound: one approved story that meets disclosure rules and turns a listing into visibility, trust and valuation.", "section": "The narrative spine.", "count": 1}, {"k": "218d953eca", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "figcaption", "cls": "", "html": "Integrated IR + PR engagement model: one narrative, two audiences, one disclosure gate.", "section": "The narrative spine.", "count": 1}, {"k": "b3db11dd7a", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "span", "cls": "num", "html": "IR lane · The investment case", "section": "The narrative spine.", "count": 1}, {"k": "3601128077", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "li", "cls": "", "html": "<strong>Audience</strong>: institutions, analysts, retail, lenders, raters", "section": "The narrative spine.", "count": 1}, {"k": "ed6075a161", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "li", "cls": "", "html": "<strong>Story</strong>: growth thesis, capital allocation, catalysts, risks", "section": "The narrative spine.", "count": 1}, {"k": "e446e97797", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "li", "cls": "", "html": "<strong>Output</strong>: results pack, IR deck, fact sheet, Q&amp;A bank", "section": "The narrative spine.", "count": 1}, {"k": "3525bd6589", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "li", "cls": "", "html": "<strong>Activities</strong>: briefings, roadshows, AGM, investor day", "section": "The narrative spine.", "count": 1}, {"k": "9c6280a387", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "li", "cls": "", "html": "<strong>Success</strong>: valuation versus peers, register quality", "section": "The narrative spine.", "count": 1}, {"k": "2127f99b50", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "span", "cls": "num", "html": "PR lane · The corporate narrative", "section": "The narrative spine.", "count": 1}, {"k": "a1efb48d2a", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "li", "cls": "", "html": "<strong>Audience</strong>: media, regulators, partners, employees, communities", "section": "The narrative spine.", "count": 1}, {"k": "cb9704fbcf", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "li", "cls": "", "html": "<strong>Story</strong>: brand credibility, leadership voice, issue positioning", "section": "The narrative spine.", "count": 1}, {"k": "cc4dd82571", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "li", "cls": "", "html": "<strong>Output</strong>: releases, media kit, spokesperson briefs, thought pieces", "section": "The narrative spine.", "count": 1}, {"k": "5a4644efb4", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "li", "cls": "", "html": "<strong>Activities</strong>: media relations, press events, op-eds, digital, crisis", "section": "The narrative spine.", "count": 1}, {"k": "5af62824ac", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "li", "cls": "", "html": "<strong>Success</strong>: share of voice, message pull-through, sentiment", "section": "The narrative spine.", "count": 1}, {"k": "ddfe163345", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "span", "cls": "n", "html": "01", "section": "The narrative spine.", "count": 2}, {"k": "3f1c632a02", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "h3", "cls": "", "html": "Diagnose", "section": "The narrative spine.", "count": 1}, {"k": "228d658b14", "scope": "approach.html", "tag": "p", "cls": "", "html": "Perception audit, risk tie